  "Question": "A cell phone plan costs \\(\\$20\\) each month, plus \\(5\\)¢ per text message sent, plus \\(10\\)¢ for each minute used over \\(30\\) hours. In January Michelle sent \\(100\\) text messages and talked for \\(30.5\\) hours. How much did she have to pay?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$24.00\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$24.50\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$25.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$28.00\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$30.00\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Only the time above \\(30\\) hours incurs an extra charge. Michelle used \\(30.5-30=0.5\\) excess hour, which is \\(0.5\\cdot60=30\\) minutes.\n\nHer \\(100\\) texts cost \\(100\\cdot\\$0.05=\\$5\\), and the extra minutes cost \\(30\\cdot\\$0.10=\\$3\\). Adding these to the monthly charge gives\n\\[\n\\$20+\\$5+\\$3=\\boxed{\\$28.00},\n\\]\nchoice D.",
